==Battleground==
*1 [[Bore]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Bakoo]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Bore]]s spawn, delay 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
**20 [[Wall Doge]]s spawn, delay 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
**1 [[Kang Roo]] spawns.

==Strategy==
The key to this stage is to abuse Bakoo's low standing range, health and very high knockback count to constantly force her back before she can even attack, then destroy everything else. You'll need either the normal cannon or Breakerblast to interrupt Bakoo's first attack. Alternatively, you can exploit her low speed by hitting the base with one unit after defeating Bore, then luring the second to your base so you can stack units without fearing further Bakoo attacks. Do not bring fast meatshields.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] - One of the best units for this stage with good stats, LD and massive damage to Red enemies. When well-supported, can tear Bore to pieces and in a small stack can accumulate enough damage to stun-lock Bakoo.
*[[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]]/[[Nymph Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Nymph Cat]] - Serves a similar purpose to Courier but only as generalist LD attackers.
*[[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]]/[[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] - Useful for dealing with Bore while you stack other units. They work better than meatshields, mostly because these keep Bore in place and allow you to actually build up momentum, reducing the risks of either it or Bakoo pushing.
*[[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] - Ironically to the stage name, Bombercat is great for disabling Bakoo and giving your units a larger damage window before Bakoo can attack again. You may want to clear out the Bores first, however.
*[[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]] - Similar to an LD unit, except with no blindspot (provided there is a stepping stone, of course). His waves can help dealing damage to Bakoo, making it easier for your other units to knock her back before she can land an attack.
*[[Brainwashed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Sexy Legs]] - Very similar to Crazed Sexy Legs, except with a surge instead of waves, which can be slightly less consistent, but it works.
*[[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Dread Pirate Catley]] - One of the very best ways to deal with the Bore. With his extremely consistent Knockback ability, high range, and quick cooldown, you can quickly build a big stack of him on the starting Bore and stack LD attackers like Courier Cat or Vaulter/Nymph Cat on it, practically disabling Bakoo once you hit the base.
*[[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]] - Can be used as crowd-control for the first Bore, he can replace iCat for this role.
*[[Matador Cat (Rare Cat)|Matador Cat]] - Can be of particular use for the first Bore, as it Dodge ability can stop him from pushing for a short while. He is also useful during the boss phase, given his naturally decent base HP.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Hattori Hanzo (Uber Rare Cat)|Hattori Hanzo]] - His fast attack rate and Freeze against Dark allows him to juggle Bakoo relatively easily. Not only that, he himself is Immune to Freeze.

