==Abyssal Strategy==
The following lineups are designed to work on their own; however, it is recommended and encouraged to add to them as you see fit. Certain [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] can dramatically simplify the stage, so don't be afraid to include them alongside these strategies.

{{Lineup
|Manic Macho Legs|30
|iCat|30
|Quarterback Cat|30
|name = Lineup 1
}}

'''Difficulty:''' ★☆☆☆☆

'''Battle:''' When Bore is about to reach your base, send out iCat to Freeze him and tank a hit. Bore will knock iCat behind the base, where you can then wait out the rest of his recharge to achieve a permafreeze. Then, stack Quarterback Cats to hell and back; they are surprisingly competent as snipers and directly target Bakoo. Once you reach about 8 of them, start spamming Manic Macho Legs and even more iCats to quickly finish off Bore and initiate the boss wave. To the save you the trouble of guessing, it is the third Quarterback hit that triggers the boss wave (second at Lv.36+ or when evolved into Gridiron Cat), so time your Cat Cannon/[[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast]] with that in mind. At this point, just keep swarming the enemies with your units and they will be put soundly to bed.

{{Lineup
|Doctor Cat
|Island Cat
|Manic Island Cat|30
|Thaumaturge Cat|30
|Elemental Duelist Cat|30
|Maglev Cat|30
|Medalist Cat|30
|Roe Cat|50
|name = Lineup 2
}}

'''Difficulty:''' ★★☆☆☆

'''Battle:''' At Lv.50, Roe Cat will have just enough effective HP to facetank if Bore is Weakened. Keep spamming Roe until two manage to stack up, then spawn a single Thaumaturge Cat and start stacking Medalist Cats. Without [[Battle Items#Rich Cat|Rich Cat]], you will barely generate enough income to support spamming both at a moderate rate, but if push comes to shove, prioritize sending out Roe first. When Bore dies, the instant income will allow you to start spamming Thaumaturge Cats for the boss wave. You don't want your Medalist Cats getting too close to the enemy base since it can ruin the chain, so cycle out Maglev Cat before they reach it (more precisely, moderately ahead of the Roes such that Bore can kill the Maglev and have some time to push up before being walled by them to prevent Bakoo from prematurely starting an attack before the last of the Medalists catch up) and time the Cat Cannon to knock Bakoo out of her attack animation, whereupon you can watch her get stunlocked to death. Cleanup after Bakoo perishes will prove too difficult for Roe and Medalist alone, so start spamming Elemental Duelist Cats and Manic Island Cats to quickly eviscerate the Bores and claim your victory.

