'''Difficulty:''' ★★★☆☆

'''Battle:''' Admittedly, the opening requires a good string of Bellydance Dodges and Enchantress Slows in order to build up a proper stack of meatshields/crowd-control. Luckily, you're able to exit out of the stage within the first 10 seconds without penalty in case things go south immediately. As soon as things are set up in the meatshielding department, start spawning in Pizza Cats to chip Bore bown while letting your units gradually build up. Once Bore dies, allow the Bellydancers to start the boss wave, but <u>don't reset Bakoo's attack animation this time</u>. You need to build enough space for your Pizza Cats to reach the frontlines before Bakoo does, so let the Kang Roo and Bore make their way to you. Start spamming Enchantress Cats alongside your other cats to make Slow procs more consistent. You've basically won by now, since Bakoo will be knocked back by every single Pizza Wave.

