'''Difficulty:''' ★★☆☆☆

'''Battle:''' Use Prof. Cat Jobs to perma-weaken Bore while he's attacking the Cat Base, then start stacking Housewife Cats. (It's possible to lose here if he dodges Prof. Cat Jobs' attack while rebounding, so keep that in mind.) Once Bore is about to bite the dust, start spamming the rest of your non-combo slaves. Courier Cat will be the one to initiate the boss wave, but <u>don't reset Bakoo's attack animation this time</u>; the space it creates is essential in allowing your units to build up and stunlock her to death. If all goes well, your Can Can Cats will hold Bore off while the rest of your piercers snipe Bakoo to death.

{{Lineup
|Jiangshi Cat
|Li'l King Dragon Cat
|Power Driller Cat
|Prof. Cat Jobs|30
|Courier Cat|30
|Awakened Bahamut Cat|40
|talent6 = Explosions Lv. 10
|name = Alternative Baha Blast strategy
|cannon = Thunderbolt
}}

'''Difficulty:''' ★★☆☆☆

'''Battle:''' Like any good Advent Stage, Talented Awakened Bahamut Cat can chain the boss to death relatively easily. Permaweaken Bore with Prof. Cat Jobs while he's attacking the Cat Base, then summon Bahamut. As soon as Bahamut kills Bore, send out a Courier Cat to get as far as possible before Bahamut finishes his backswing. Start spamming Jiangshi Cats too.

The following sequence of events should play out in order:

#Bahamut hits the base, creating an Explosion that kills most of the starting peons.
#He rebounds from the boss shockwave, then hits Bore.
#Bore hits him.
#'''Use your Thunderbolt here, that way Bahamut doesn't get hit by Bore again on the following attack.'''
#Bahamut recoils, hitting Bore again and causing him to stagger.
#Your Courier Cat moves in front of Bahamut, briefly protecting him from taking another hit.
#Bahamut and Bore exchange hits at the same time.
#Bahamut rebounds onto Bore, finally killing him and leaving Bakoo open.

One last Baha Blast should take care of her. Try to take out the enemy base before Bore #2 spawns. If your Bahamut is Lv.50, an entirely different chain will play out, but it should still lead to an identical situation (with Bore dead). However, the Thunderbolt timing needs to be adjusted to after Bore's first stagger.

