==Trivia==
*Bombergirl's seemingly arbitrary name is a pun that only works in Japanese. The Japanese word for bomb, ''bakudan'', happens to contain the word ''baku'', which can refer to either a [[wikipedia:Malayan tapir|Malayan tapir]], or a [[wikipedia:Baku (mythology)|dream-eating mythical creature]], both of which served as inspirations for [[Bakoo]]'s design.
*Deeply Dreaming's Japanese name is "Yoru wa Mijikashi Yume Miyo Otome" (夜は短し夢見よ乙女), which can be translated as "Night Is Short, Dream On Maiden"; this is a reference to the novel and animated film ''[[wikipedia:Night Is Short, Walk On Girl|Night Is Short, Walk On Girl]]'' (夜は短し歩けよ乙女), which in turn are based on the 1915 ballad "[[wikipedia:Gondola no Uta|Gondola no Uta]]".

